{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvaejJAy7rJugFc4QaAs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: retire the widget, and don't run the diary study to make this decision.**\n\n**Why retire it:**\n- **Few users:** after a full year, only 1.1% of weekly iOS users have added it.\n- **No measurable benefit:** widget users retain the same as matched users without it. For a habit tracker, retention is the main thing a widget should improve, and it doesn't.\n- **High cost:** it adds about three days of QA to every iOS release, and keeping it means a five-week rewrite. Those weeks could go to something with a proven effect.\n- **Natural end date:** Apple retiring the API forces a decision anyway, so you can drop it cleanly instead of maintaining it indefinitely.\n\n**Why not the diary study:** It answers a different question: what a good widget would look like. You need to decide whether this widget is worth five weeks plus ongoing QA, and your data already answers that. A study would also delay you while the API deadline gets closer.\n\n**Do these quick checks before committing (days, not weeks):**\n1. Do widget users skew toward paying subscribers or higher lifetime value? If so, revenue matters more than their retention numbers suggest.\n2. Check App Store reviews and support tickets for how much people mention the widget.\n3. Confirm the retention match covered engagement before users added the widget, not just demographics.\n\n**If those checks come back clean:**\n- Give widget users notice in the app.\n- Remove the widget well before Apple's cutoff.\n- Reclaim the QA time.\n\nIf widgets later become strategic, for example interactive check-ins from the home screen, the designer's research becomes worthwhile as discovery for a new product. It isn't a reason to keep the current one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3195,"cache_read_input_tokens":5037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3195},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ae4ac8-5aba-422b-a2ce-1afa94b59bf9","uuid":"d67f0511-217f-48ee-9111-0f5b9ea01592","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:08:21.429Z","request_id":"req_011CfvaeiwLU9A9tLDgDJwtp"}
